From f0e25e3ef330c317a6caf6f64962bf53c04449fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: spelliott <spelliott@devvm11359.lla0.facebook.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Mar 2026 03:05:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] [rootcanal] Disable ASAN for darwin builds

Summary:
I was trying out a combination of Bluetooth/netsim related options which mean we try to launch `root-canal`.  This has a dependency on an ASAN library which we don't include in the build, likely we do not even need ASAN for this build.

The error logs in `launcher.log` look like P2249731370

Test Plan: @jeffreyeffendy I think just being able to build and boot Tiki CF N16 with the default options should be enough? I don't think we touch rootcanal unless we start explicitly disabling netsim etc like I have been trying out.

Reviewers: jeffreyeffendy, achong, divyesh07, #wearables-vanilla-aosp, #wearables_emulators, pakhomov, dougyoung, krishnaprasadmv, nsavant

Reviewed By: jeffreyeffendy

Subscribers: jeffreyeffendy, jessiew, #wearables_emulators

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.intern.facebook.com/D98288587

Tags: connectivity-bt-transport-shiproom-pending
---
 tools/rootcanal/Android.bp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tools/rootcanal/Android.bp b/tools/rootcanal/Android.bp
index de61f72a82..5c74568bab 100644
--- a/tools/rootcanal/Android.bp
+++ b/tools/rootcanal/Android.bp
@@ -396,6 +396,10 @@ cc_binary_host {
         },
         darwin: {
             enabled: true,
+            sanitize: {
+                address: false,
+                all_undefined: false,
+            },
         },
     },
 }
